<title>USA: Intel invests in new Samsung chip plant.</title>
<headline>Intel invests in new Samsung chip plant.</headline>
<dateline>AUSTIN, Texas 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Samsung Electronics Co said on Thursday that Intel Corp is making an equity investment in Samsung's new advanced-memory plant in Texas.</p>
<p>Samsung will retain full management of the $1.3 billion Austin plant, scheduled to begin production in late 1997. It will supply Intel with memory products under the terms of the agreement.</p>
<p>Samsung Electronics, a unit of Korea's Samsung Group, said earlier this month it was considering cutting production of memory chips this year due to low prices.</p>
<p>The exact amount of Intel's investment in the new plant was not disclosed.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
